This version evaluates both pointer checks with a non-short-circuit `&` instead of `&&`. Both checks are side-effect-free, so the result is identical. The compiler can then produce a branchless pair of compare-and-set instructions.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL DeveloperFieldDefinition::IsDefined() const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>((nullptr != mesg) & (nullptr != developer));
}
```